A||||13||Jackalrr||Best sub location in a Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||Jackalrr||12-15-2000||03:43 PM||||Has anyone tried putting a sub or two up in the front trunk? If so, does it work well and is it worth it? I really want to get some subs in my car but I would prefer not to do any cutting on the car.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||286SE'S||12-15-2000||04:03 PM||||There have been lots of suggestions in the past about adding subs. Use the search function and look for 'subs' or 'subwoofer'.<BR>General problem with a sub in the front trunk is you can't hear it in the car and it rattles the hood. Great for shows. You have to vent it into the car interior somehow and that is the 'cutting' you don't want to do.||||reg||7
Z||000002||KRMFiero||12-15-2000||04:14 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  - go there<BR>also go to West Coast Fiero's website<P><BR>Umm Incase you want to know:<BR>sub in back trunk - will not feel anything<BR>sub in front trunk w/o port - hood rattles, will get some bass, NOT alot<BR>sub in center consil - loud, good bass<P>there's my unuseful information<P>also might want to look at the World wide Fiero links site<P>Kyle<BR><P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-15-2000||04:16 PM||||check out stimpy's footwell sub. it's a pretty good idea i think. only a 10 can fit, but if you get a good one i think it'll do just fine.<P>just my 2 1/2 cents.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Stoic||12-15-2000||05:14 PM||||I have a 10" sub under the dash.  No footwell obstruction, not even in view unless you climb in and look up.  As soon as I get a scanner I'll post a pic.||||reg||6
Z||000005||kornholio||12-15-2000||05:50 PM||||This is where my sub is...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sub1_2.jpg"> <P>When I have passengers, I have to put the sub facing up to have enough leg room.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||12-15-2000||07:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>check out stimpy's footwell sub. it's a pretty good idea i think. only a 10 can fit, but if you get a good one i think it'll do just fine.<P>just my 2 1/2 cents.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the good word, Adam. Here's a pic of what we are talkin about...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high">  <P>And it is very easy to make. As you can see, this sealed fiberglass and wood enclosure takes up no more footroom on the passenger side then the pedals take up for the driver, equaling basically no loss of useable footroom for passenger, plus plenty of clean, unobstructed bass.||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||12-15-2000||10:46 PM||||Yup, I just did the same set up as Stimpys..(saw the pic from an earlier post)...works and looks great! Def. the way to go...(pics to come after I carpet it).<BR>BTW Stimpy, what kind of sub did you use? I used a Pioneer sub (10 inch) w/ a 100 watt Pioneer amp..perfect sound..not too annoying, just added enough bass to offset the tweeters I installed overhead...<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 12-15-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||fropuff||12-15-2000||11:32 PM||||Yep, I also built stimpy's box.  Very easy if you know fiberglass.  It makes it a LOT easier to lay the cloth down, then brush the resin on with a small paint brush.  Not nearly as messy and you don't get as itchy.  I built mine to fit an 8.  Actually to fit a 10, but it's a little small.  Mine will be a little shallower than stimpy's.  Won't need much of an amp either.  I don't need the best system anyway.  Just have to beat that little retard with the 94 Probe!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||12-16-2000||11:28 AM||||mine is also like stimpy's, but smaller and holds an 8" because i thought it might take up too much room. now i'm tryng to augment it with a couple more in the doors (circuit cities' still looking for my 12 ohm 8's). probaly if i do another for the indy i'll go a little larger and add a ten too.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierosound||12-16-2000||03:15 PM||||I've had great success with subs behind each seat.  Others here at PFF have followed my lead with excellent results as well.  See the forum  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003613.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003613.html</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000011||stimpy||12-16-2000||07:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Stimpy, what kind of sub did you use?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> I used a Polk Audio dX10 with a no name 440w amp bridged to mono. I'm sure the speaker could handle plenty more power (I really like 1FST2M6's xtant amp... drewl) but it does the job plety fine as is.  Fierosounds' set up looks very clean and I'm sure it sounds great, but cutting just wasn't in the equation for me. Plus, with no seat to fire through, the sound is very crisp. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Stoic||12-16-2000||07:53 PM||||Fierosound:<BR>Very nice!  Does the depth of the box vary from the top to the bottom?<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I,m parked.||||reg||1
Z||000013||MachineHead||12-17-2000||02:36 PM||||I definitely wouldn't put a sub in one of the trunks.  Stimpy's box is cool, and fierosounds is really neat if you are capable of doing it.<P>BTW, nice choice in Subs FieroSounds!||||reg||1
